## Executive Summary
A controlled security exercise was conducted to simulate suspicious Windows endpoint and account-management activity. The exercise generated PowerShell, Command Prompt, Certutil, Active Directory account-creation, and local administrative-group modification telemetry.

The activity was detected and investigated using Splunk, Windows Security logs, Sysmon, and PowerShell Script Block Logging.

## Initial Indicators
- PowerShell process execution
- Windows Command Shell execution
- Certutil execution
- Creation of `s12_incident`
- Addition of `s12_incident` to local Administrators

## Severity
