## Investigation
The analyst reviewed process-creation telemetry, PowerShell script blocks, account-management events, and local-group membership changes.

The observed sequence indicated command execution followed by account creation and privilege assignment.

## Findings
- PowerShell and CMD activity originated from WIN11-01.
- Certutil was used to hash a legitimate Windows executable.
- A new domain account was created on DC01.
- The account was added to the local Administrators group on WIN11-01.
- The activity was authorized as part of the controlled exercise.

## Containment
- Removed the test account from local Administrators.

## Remediation
- Deleted the temporary Active Directory account.
- Removed test artifacts.
- Verified approved administrator membership.
- Confirmed telemetry remained operational.

## Disposition
Benign – Authorized Security Exercise

